{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ClassicalLimitObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ClassicalLimitObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.descartes_kummer_5_persists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.descartes_kummer_5_persists","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ClassicalLimitObstruction.lean#L115-L117","doc":"5 does not divide χ(A) = -6: the obstruction persists at level 5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.descartes_kummer_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.descartes_kummer_3","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ClassicalLimitObstruction.lean#L111-L113","doc":"3 divides χ(A) = -6 in the Descartes universe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.descartes_kummer_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.descartes_kummer_2","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ClassicalLimitObstruction.lean#L107-L109","doc":"2 divides χ(A) = -6 in the Descartes universe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.descartesObstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.descartesObstruction","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ClassicalLimitObstruction.lean#L100-L105","doc":"For the Descartes universe, `χ(A) = -6`.\nThe divisors of 6 are `{1, 2, 3, 6}`, so the obstruction\nvanishes at exactly these four Kummer levels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.kummer_obstruction_divisibility","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.kummer_obstruction_divisibility","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ClassicalLimitObstruction.lean#L85-L98","doc":"The obstruction vanishes at Kummer level `n` iff `n ∣ χ(A)`.\n\nFor the Descartes universe with `χ(A) = -6`, the obstruction\nvanishes only at `n ∈ {1, 2, 3, 6}` and persists at all\nother levels — in particular at all primes > 3.\n\nRef: [yekutieli2010] https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2010.03.006 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qou_obstruction_one_dimensional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qou_obstruction_one_dimensional","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ClassicalLimitObstruction.lean#L77-L83","doc":"In a QOU, the obstruction space constructed via `ofQOU` is\none-dimensional (by construction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ClassicalLimitObstruction.ofQOU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ClassicalLimitObstruction.ofQOU","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ClassicalLimitObstruction.lean#L59-L75","doc":"Construct the classical limit obstruction for a QOU.\n\nIn a QOU, the obstruction space is one-dimensional:\n- Observability gives `HH⁰(Ad) = 0`.\n- Frobenius–Poincaré duality gives `HH² ≅ (HH¹)∨`.\n- Drinfeld uniqueness gives `dim HH¹ = 1`.\n- Therefore `dim HH² = 1`.\n\nThe generator maps to `χ(A)` under the trace map.\n\nRef: [yekutieli2010] https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2010.03.006 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ClassicalLimitObstruction.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ClassicalLimitObstruction.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ClassicalLimitObstruction.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The Euler characteristic of the base curve, `χ_eu(M₀) = 2 − 2g`,\nto which the generator of the obstruction line pairs under the\nWigner axiom.  (This field read \"`χ(A) = tr(id_A)`\" until 2026-09-15;\n`tr(id_A)` is the quantum dimension of `A`, a different object.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ClassicalLimitObstruction.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ClassicalLimitObstruction.dim","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ClassicalLimitObstruction.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The dimension of the obstruction space `HH²(Ad)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ClassicalLimitObstruction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ClassicalLimitObstruction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ClassicalLimitObstruction.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ClassicalLimitObstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ClassicalLimitObstruction","kind":"structure","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ClassicalLimitObstruction.lean#L43-L57","doc":"The **classical limit obstruction space** of a quantum universe.\n\nFor a general QU, this is `HH²(𝒰_q, Ad)` — potentially\nmulti-dimensional.  For a QOU, the observability axiom and\nFrobenius duality reduce it to a one-dimensional space.\n\nThe generator maps to `χ(A) ∈ ℤ` under the trace map. ","signatureChunk":0}]}